  "goodToKnow": "Das Trinkwasser is drinking water. In Germany, tap water (Leitungswasser) is strictly regulated by the Trinkwasserverordnung and is generally safe to drink, though many Germans still prefer bottled Mineralwasser, often sparkling (mit Kohlensäure or Sprudel). A sign saying Kein Trinkwasser warns you not to drink from that tap. In restaurants, asking for free Leitungswasser is less common than in some countries, and you may be charged."
